{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1766,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "It's gone. The Queen's necklace vanished from a locked throne room.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 82
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Every door was bolted. So the thief is one of these twelve guards.",
   "from": 86,
   "to": 188
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The King locks them in and hands each guard the same wooden stick.",
   "from": 191,
   "to": 287
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "king",
   "text": "These are my wizard's sticks. Tonight, the thief's stick grows one inch.",
   "from": 290,
   "to": 454
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "One guard can't stop grinning.",
   "from": 457,
   "to": 495
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "thief",
   "text": "Then measure mine first!",
   "from": 499,
   "to": 551
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "king",
   "text": "Tomorrow.",
   "from": 554,
   "to": 576
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "All night, the guards stare at their sticks.",
   "from": 579,
   "to": 660
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "At midnight, one measures his against the floor tiles.",
   "from": 664,
   "to": 750
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Another holds his up to a snoring friend's stick.",
   "from": 753,
   "to": 813
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But the grinning guard hides his stick inside his jacket.",
   "from": 817,
   "to": 883
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Just before sunrise, a faint scraping comes from the corner. Then silence.",
   "from": 886,
   "to": 988
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "By morning, the guards lay their sticks side by side.",
   "from": 991,
   "to": 1065
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Eleven match perfectly. One is shorter.",
   "from": 1068,
   "to": 1150
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "thief",
   "text": "That's impossible! It was supposed to grow!",
   "from": 1166,
   "to": 1240
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He freezes. Too late.",
   "from": 1244,
   "to": 1280
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "king",
   "text": "The necklace.",
   "from": 1284,
   "to": 1324
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Here's the trick. These were never a wizard's sticks.",
   "from": 1327,
   "to": 1408
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They came from the palace woodshed. No stick could ever grow.",
   "from": 1412,
   "to": 1491
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So the innocent guards had no reason to touch theirs.",
   "from": 1495,
   "to": 1570
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Only the thief believed. So he shaved one inch off the end.",
   "from": 1574,
   "to": 1649
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The King never measured anything. The thief did it for him.",
   "from": 1653,
   "to": 1742
  }
 ],
